  beschreibung: Uranus is an ice giant with a pale blue-green color caused by methane
    in its atmosphere. Its rotation axis is tilted almost sideways, so the planet
    seems to roll around the Sun like a ball. This creates extremely long seasons,
    with one pole receiving sunlight for many years while the other remains in darkness.
    Uranus has narrow, dark rings and many moons.
  planetSizeInfoText: Uranus is about four times as wide as Earth and belongs to
    the ice giants.
  orbitalDistanceInfoText: Uranus orbits the Sun at about 19.19 AU. Sunlight takes
    more than two and a half hours to get there.
  orbitalSpeedInfoText: One orbit takes about 84 Earth years, so Uranus moves very
    slowly around the Sun.
  axialTiltInfoText: Uranus is tilted almost sideways, so its poles point toward
    or away from the Sun for long periods.
  eccentricityInfoText: Uranus' orbit is only slightly elliptical. The extreme impression
    mainly comes from its tilted axis.
  planetScaleInfoText: Compared with Earth, Uranus is a large planet, but it is much
    smaller than Jupiter and Saturn.
  gravityInfoText: Gravity is slightly below Earth's gravity. At the cloud tops,
    you would be a little lighter than on Earth.
  fakten:
  - Uranus has no true solid surface; its visible layer is atmosphere above deeper fluids.
  - Uranus gets its blue-green color from methane, which absorbs red light.
  - Uranus is tilted almost sideways and seems to roll around the Sun.
